1
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:41,547
This is a full-on retreat! Everyone get to the airport!

2
00:01:43,407 --> 00:01:46,087
The escape helicopter should be waiting for us.

3
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:49,007
All right, then, let's fall back.

4
00:01:51,267 --> 00:01:53,507
Do whatever it takes to get there alive!

5
00:01:59,727 --> 00:02:00,527
Move it!

6
00:02:01,007 --> 00:02:02,007
Go!

7
00:02:03,467 --> 00:02:04,467
Stop!

8
00:02:05,947 --> 00:02:08,347
её!

9
00:02:09,547 --> 00:02:10,287
I saw you

10
00:02:19,907 --> 00:02:23,207
Racketcumulac!

11
00:02:25,727 --> 00:02:26,987
He went.

12
00:02:26,987 --> 00:02:44,807
Damn it.

13
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:56,387
You, hey, listen to me.

14
00:02:56,987 --> 00:03:00,307
You're not safe out here in the open, and I can't keep carrying you.

15
00:03:00,507 --> 00:03:02,027
You've got to open your eyes and get up.

16
00:03:02,187 --> 00:03:03,207
You, come on!

17
00:03:04,967 --> 00:03:05,807
Wake up!

18
00:03:11,407 --> 00:03:12,547
I'm not healing.

19
00:03:13,327 --> 00:03:14,867
At this rate, I'm going to.

20
00:03:14,867 --> 00:03:23,547
Let's get up.

21
00:03:24,707 --> 00:03:27,227
Ah!

22
00:03:33,867 --> 00:03:34,327
Ah!

23
00:03:34,327 --> 00:03:44,147
Please, help me!

24
00:03:44,147 --> 00:03:46,467
You guys, he's gonna kill me!

25
00:03:47,987 --> 00:03:49,287
Run away!

26
00:03:54,687 --> 00:03:56,067
No, stop!

27
00:03:57,667 --> 00:04:00,147
Blood, I just need a little...

28
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:06,327
New monster!

29
00:04:34,327 --> 00:04:37,907
Blood, I just need a little...

30
00:04:38,407 --> 00:04:38,907
Ugh...

31
00:04:38,907 --> 00:04:40,407
Ugh...

32
00:04:40,407 --> 00:04:59,067
Your devotion to those you care about is overwhelming.

33
00:04:59,447 --> 00:05:03,827
When your family's in danger of being harmed, you lose all sense of right and wrong.

34
00:05:04,867 --> 00:05:08,407
That's gonna get us in trouble one of these days, don't you think, you?

35
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:11,567
What am I doing here?

36
00:05:12,347 --> 00:05:13,947
Please don't tell me I'm dead again.

37
00:05:14,307 --> 00:05:16,407
Not this time. You've been knocked unconscious.

38
00:05:18,927 --> 00:05:21,627
Wait, Gurren! What happened back there?

39
00:05:22,747 --> 00:05:24,787
See, this is what I was talking about.

40
00:05:25,027 --> 00:05:26,847
You're always obsessing over someone.

41
00:05:27,227 --> 00:05:31,127
Yeah, whatever. Just tell me Gurren, Shinoa, and the others are fine.

42
00:05:31,607 --> 00:05:33,247
I have no idea if they are.

43
00:05:33,247 --> 00:05:37,147
I can only see what you see, and your eyes have been closed for a while now.

44
00:05:37,267 --> 00:05:39,507
Then, they might still have Gurren.

45
00:05:39,907 --> 00:05:41,667
Gurren? Yeah, sure.

46
00:05:42,367 --> 00:05:45,867
But it's a different member of your family you should be worried about.

47
00:05:59,107 --> 00:06:01,147
Where am I? Hello?

48
00:06:03,247 --> 00:06:17,067
It can't be.

49
00:06:18,207 --> 00:06:18,967
No way.

50
00:06:19,407 --> 00:06:20,887
Mika, is that you?

51
00:06:20,887 --> 00:06:26,267
Mika!

52
00:06:26,267 --> 00:06:26,347
Mika!

53
00:06:33,347 --> 00:06:35,147
Stop! What are you doing?

54
00:06:35,287 --> 00:06:35,667
Blood.

55
00:06:35,947 --> 00:06:36,487
Come on!

56
00:06:36,707 --> 00:06:38,047
I need to drink some blood!

57
00:06:38,707 --> 00:06:39,107
It...

58
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:40,687
It hurts.

59
00:06:41,407 --> 00:06:42,787
Hey, what's happening?

60
00:06:43,267 --> 00:06:45,247
Mika can't fight it!

61
00:06:45,247 --> 00:06:46,607
I need blood!

62
00:06:46,887 --> 00:06:48,267
The thirst is too painful!

63
00:06:48,607 --> 00:06:49,647
I can't take it!

64
00:06:53,027 --> 00:06:54,647
I'm so sorry, Mika.

65
00:06:56,707 --> 00:06:57,847
It's my fault.

66
00:06:58,467 --> 00:07:00,007
I shouldn't have left you all alone.

67
00:07:00,007 --> 00:07:16,247
What did I almost do?

68
00:07:17,467 --> 00:07:17,947
Sorry.

69
00:07:18,607 --> 00:07:20,327
I wasn't myself just now.

70
00:07:21,047 --> 00:07:22,207
Is it really that bad?

71
00:07:22,207 --> 00:07:23,907
If you don't drink blood, I mean.

72
00:07:26,787 --> 00:07:28,767
This is all because I left you behind.

73
00:07:29,207 --> 00:07:31,207
No, like I told you before, I...

74
00:07:31,207 --> 00:07:36,307
Mika!

75
00:07:38,807 --> 00:07:40,087
No, stay back.

76
00:07:40,827 --> 00:07:44,027
I don't want to hurt you, and I don't trust myself right now.

77
00:07:44,107 --> 00:07:44,887
But you're hurt.

78
00:07:44,887 --> 00:07:46,467
Don't worry about yourself, not me!

79
00:07:47,747 --> 00:07:50,887
Besides, there are some things we need to talk about.

80
00:07:51,027 --> 00:07:52,767
Whatever you have to say can wait, damn it!

81
00:07:53,267 --> 00:07:55,347
I just got you back, and now you're gonna die?

82
00:07:55,527 --> 00:07:56,447
You can't do that!

83
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:57,907
Please don't leave me, Mika!

84
00:07:59,867 --> 00:08:00,927
Blood will heal you.

85
00:08:02,647 --> 00:08:03,647
Take what you need.

86
00:08:05,107 --> 00:08:05,767
Do it.

87
00:08:10,567 --> 00:08:12,427
Please, you have to stay away from me.

88
00:08:12,787 --> 00:08:13,947
I can't keep fighting.

89
00:08:13,947 --> 00:08:15,607
It's too powerful.

90
00:08:19,887 --> 00:08:20,867
Just do it.

91
00:08:21,587 --> 00:08:24,687
If it's gonna save you, then drink all you want.

92
00:08:28,407 --> 00:08:29,287
What's the matter?

93
00:08:29,547 --> 00:08:30,327
Hey, come on.

94
00:08:30,607 --> 00:08:31,627
We've been reunited.

95
00:08:32,267 --> 00:08:32,667
Finally.

96
00:08:33,327 --> 00:08:35,307
I'm not going to lose you again, Mika.

97
00:08:35,407 --> 00:08:36,087
I can't.

98
00:08:36,387 --> 00:08:36,907
I won't.

99
00:08:37,127 --> 00:08:38,227
No, you don't understand.

100
00:08:38,707 --> 00:08:40,407
There's no going back if I do that.

101
00:08:40,407 --> 00:08:46,127
If I drink human blood, even a drop, I'll be a complete vampire.

102
00:08:46,667 --> 00:08:48,447
One who will never age.

103
00:08:48,767 --> 00:08:51,147
There won't be a shred of humanity left in me.

104
00:08:51,147 --> 00:08:53,847
Okay, but that still means it'll save you.

105
00:08:54,227 --> 00:08:55,867
We won't be separated again.

106
00:08:55,867 --> 00:08:58,467
Hey, come on.

107
00:08:58,727 --> 00:09:01,707
Can't you just do me this one tiny favor and stay alive?

108
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:04,607
I can't.

109
00:09:04,807 --> 00:09:05,647
Wrong answer.

110
00:09:06,067 --> 00:09:08,287
If you don't want to do it, I'll have to make you.

111
00:09:08,527 --> 00:09:09,807
I said no, dammit!

112
00:09:09,807 --> 00:09:17,027
I've been fighting it so long, with everything in my power.

113
00:09:17,467 --> 00:09:18,767
I don't want to be a monster.

114
00:09:19,247 --> 00:09:21,687
I don't want you to see me as some grotesque creature.

115
00:09:23,267 --> 00:09:25,127
So I've swallowed down my thirst.

116
00:09:25,407 --> 00:09:26,227
It wasn't easy.

117
00:09:26,787 --> 00:09:28,187
And now you're telling me-

118
00:09:28,187 --> 00:09:29,587
Of course it's not easy, dummy!

119
00:09:29,947 --> 00:09:32,827
Do you really think I want to watch my best friend turn into a vampire?

120
00:09:33,267 --> 00:09:35,587
But tell me, Mika, what other choice do I have?

121
00:09:35,587 --> 00:09:39,227
If you die here, then I'll-

122
00:09:39,227 --> 00:09:39,887
I'll-

123
00:09:39,887 --> 00:09:42,067
I'll have to start crying!

124
00:09:44,587 --> 00:09:45,947
You've gotta be kidding me.

125
00:09:46,507 --> 00:09:48,507
I don't care if you become a monster.

126
00:09:48,907 --> 00:09:49,647
You'll survive.

127
00:09:49,907 --> 00:09:51,667
So just suck it up and do it for me!

128
00:09:52,287 --> 00:09:53,607
You can't be serious.

129
00:09:53,727 --> 00:09:56,347
You want me to become a vampire so you don't have to cry?

130
00:09:56,527 --> 00:09:57,207
Yeah, I do.

131
00:09:57,267 --> 00:09:58,427
You got a problem with that?

132
00:10:00,187 --> 00:10:00,587
Yeah.

133
00:10:01,127 --> 00:10:03,387
Jeez, you haven't changed a bit since we were kids.

134
00:10:03,807 --> 00:10:04,647
I'm offering.

135
00:10:04,647 --> 00:10:06,207
It's not like you're attacking me.

136
00:10:07,307 --> 00:10:10,747
Besides, I don't know if I believe you really fought it all that hard

137
00:10:10,747 --> 00:10:13,627
if you're willing to die even though survival is right in front of you.

138
00:10:14,007 --> 00:10:17,007
If you wanted to die, then you should have done it in secret somewhere.

139
00:10:17,287 --> 00:10:17,787
Listen, you.

140
00:10:18,227 --> 00:10:20,727
I'm here because you need to know what the humans are-

141
00:10:20,727 --> 00:10:22,167
La la la la la la!

142
00:10:22,227 --> 00:10:23,567
I can't hear you, Mika!

143
00:10:23,947 --> 00:10:24,507
Come on.

144
00:10:24,827 --> 00:10:25,487
Please listen.

145
00:10:25,987 --> 00:10:28,167
Okay, but only if you'll agree to drink my blood.

146
00:10:28,167 --> 00:10:35,687
Stay alive for me.

147
00:10:41,947 --> 00:10:43,707
I refuse to let you die.

148
00:10:44,387 --> 00:10:46,207
Just go ahead and give in to your thirst.

149
00:10:46,207 --> 00:11:08,827
You know, you're an awful person.

150
00:11:08,827 --> 00:11:09,467
Maybe.

151
00:11:10,127 --> 00:11:13,327
But you've only got yourself to blame for making me your family.

152
00:11:14,167 --> 00:11:15,907
Biggest mistake of my life.

153
00:11:16,427 --> 00:11:18,407
I'm gonna become a monster because of you.

154
00:11:19,607 --> 00:11:21,107
I'm gonna keep living.

155
00:11:21,687 --> 00:11:24,747
We'll still be family, no matter what you become.

156
00:11:24,747 --> 00:11:34,707
I'm sorry.

157
00:11:35,587 --> 00:11:37,287
It's so hard to resist.

158
00:11:38,107 --> 00:11:40,547
I want to drink blood so badly.

159
00:11:40,547 --> 00:11:40,647
I want to drink blood so badly.

160
00:11:54,747 --> 00:12:15,187
Welcome back, Mika.

161
00:12:24,747 --> 00:12:45,447
It's weird, right?

162
00:12:46,007 --> 00:12:46,747
All of this.

163
00:12:47,247 --> 00:12:47,707
Everything.

164
00:12:48,027 --> 00:12:50,047
Drinking your family's blood just to stay alive.

165
00:12:50,347 --> 00:12:51,387
It's not normal.

166
00:12:52,207 --> 00:12:53,067
So what?

167
00:12:53,067 --> 00:12:55,107
Like we care about being normal.

168
00:12:56,587 --> 00:12:57,367
That's true.

169
00:12:57,807 --> 00:12:58,847
Still, it's strange.

170
00:13:00,127 --> 00:13:02,127
Never thought I'd become a real vampire.

171
00:13:04,987 --> 00:13:07,887
You know, reminds me of something Gurren said.

172
00:13:08,267 --> 00:13:08,527
Gurren?

173
00:13:09,067 --> 00:13:09,507
Oh, yeah.

174
00:13:09,787 --> 00:13:11,287
I forgot you don't know everyone.

175
00:13:11,847 --> 00:13:14,887
He's the army guy who found me after I escaped from the vampires.

176
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:16,587
He took me in and cared for me.

177
00:13:16,787 --> 00:13:19,087
He likes to talk, and he gives good advice.

178
00:13:19,087 --> 00:13:24,507
He told me to keep on living, even if it was just for revenge.

179
00:13:25,587 --> 00:13:30,427
That one day, someone who needed my help would show up and give me a new reason to exist.

180
00:13:31,307 --> 00:13:32,827
That's why I'm still alive.

181
00:13:33,787 --> 00:13:35,407
Even when life felt pointless.

182
00:13:36,087 --> 00:13:37,807
Even when I thought no one needed me.

183
00:13:37,807 --> 00:13:40,667
I forced myself to get through each day.

184
00:13:41,927 --> 00:13:42,847
And I'm glad.

185
00:13:44,047 --> 00:13:46,107
Because I finally got to see you again.

186
00:13:48,867 --> 00:13:50,267
Hey, let's make a promise.

187
00:13:50,767 --> 00:13:53,367
We'll survive together, even if it's painful sometimes.

188
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:55,967
Who cares if you're a vampire?

189
00:13:56,407 --> 00:13:59,687
If it's too difficult for you, then I'll just have to turn you back into a human.

190
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:06,487
So please, promise me you won't give up and try to die ever again.

191
00:14:07,707 --> 00:14:08,647
Oh, the irony.

192
00:14:09,327 --> 00:14:12,407
I fought all this time because I thought you needed saving.

193
00:14:13,547 --> 00:14:15,007
But you're the strong one.

194
00:14:15,487 --> 00:14:17,107
Guess you have changed in some ways.

195
00:14:17,367 --> 00:14:17,627
What?

196
00:14:17,827 --> 00:14:19,687
Come on, I've always been the strong one.

197
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:22,207
No, you used to be a real big crybaby.

198
00:14:22,207 --> 00:14:23,047
Huh?

199
00:14:23,227 --> 00:14:25,087
You're the one who's bawling right now!

200
00:14:31,627 --> 00:14:32,987
Okay, you got me there.

201
00:14:33,387 --> 00:14:38,587
Well, if you really think I'm stronger than before, then it's probably all because of Gurren's training.

202
00:14:38,907 --> 00:14:42,487
You may think that, but this Gurren guy you keep talking about is just using you...

203
00:14:42,487 --> 00:14:43,807
I know he's got his own plans.

204
00:14:44,827 --> 00:14:46,567
But he's part of my family, too.

205
00:14:47,527 --> 00:14:50,087
I was as good as dead when my parents abandoned me.

206
00:14:50,087 --> 00:14:51,647
I thought life was over.

207
00:14:51,647 --> 00:14:55,347
But you and Gurren both made me want to keep living.

208
00:14:56,407 --> 00:14:58,247
You guys are the only reason I'm here today.

209
00:14:59,247 --> 00:15:00,047
So you see?

210
00:15:00,467 --> 00:15:03,227
I can never pay either of you back for all that you've done.

211
00:15:03,387 --> 00:15:04,747
So I don't mind if you use me.

212
00:15:05,007 --> 00:15:07,187
I'm nothing like those human bastards, you.

213
00:15:07,647 --> 00:15:09,907
I'd never manipulate you the way that they are.

214
00:15:09,907 --> 00:15:12,647
You say that, but you did drink my blood.

215
00:15:13,167 --> 00:15:13,647
Yeah.

216
00:15:14,287 --> 00:15:15,727
I'm just messing with you.

217
00:15:16,147 --> 00:15:17,347
I don't care about the blood.

218
00:15:18,567 --> 00:15:20,747
But I do have a small favor to ask.

219
00:15:21,227 --> 00:15:22,007
What is it?

220
00:15:22,007 --> 00:15:23,427
My teammates.

221
00:15:24,087 --> 00:15:25,507
My family is in trouble.

222
00:15:26,227 --> 00:15:27,367
Please, come with me.

223
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:28,247
Okay?

224
00:15:28,247 --> 00:15:30,427
No, wait.

225
00:15:30,487 --> 00:15:30,907
Hold on.

226
00:15:31,407 --> 00:15:32,227
What are you doing?

227
00:15:32,487 --> 00:15:33,367
Think about this.

228
00:15:34,367 --> 00:15:36,267
You can't go back to those humans.

229
00:15:36,267 --> 00:15:45,247
Just hear me out first.

230
00:15:45,407 --> 00:15:46,187
I'm begging you.

231
00:15:46,367 --> 00:15:47,307
This isn't good.

232
00:15:48,107 --> 00:15:49,587
How long have I been out for?

233
00:15:50,087 --> 00:15:50,787
Please, you.

234
00:15:51,787 --> 00:15:52,107
Mika.

235
00:15:53,007 --> 00:15:54,727
You're the one who carried me out here.

236
00:15:55,567 --> 00:15:58,827
That means you must have some idea of what happened to my teammates.

237
00:15:59,427 --> 00:16:02,607
Would you stop worrying about those humans and start paying attention to me?

238
00:16:03,567 --> 00:16:06,647
I don't know what kind of awful brainwashing they've put you through.

239
00:16:07,547 --> 00:16:09,487
But I can't let you go back to the army.

240
00:16:10,187 --> 00:16:10,867
They're evil.

241
00:16:11,227 --> 00:16:13,927
They've been experimenting on you and me since we were just kids.

242
00:16:14,467 --> 00:16:15,047
See ya.

243
00:16:17,607 --> 00:16:19,107
Why won't you listen to me?

244
00:16:20,107 --> 00:16:21,447
You can't stop me.

245
00:16:22,947 --> 00:16:23,427
Fine.

246
00:16:30,467 --> 00:16:31,587
What are you doing?

247
00:16:32,307 --> 00:16:34,007
Did you really pull a sword on me?

248
00:16:35,047 --> 00:16:37,267
I'll do whatever it takes to protect you.

249
00:16:37,927 --> 00:16:40,207
If that's the case, then you should be helping me.

250
00:16:41,767 --> 00:16:42,447
Helping you?

251
00:16:45,067 --> 00:16:46,807
Kill me if you don't want me to go.

252
00:16:47,407 --> 00:16:50,167
Because I'd rather die than fail to protect my family.

253
00:16:50,167 --> 00:16:52,307
You're such a hypocrite.

254
00:16:52,627 --> 00:16:55,367
You said I had to survive even if it meant becoming a vampire.

255
00:16:55,707 --> 00:16:55,727
Mika.

256
00:16:56,567 --> 00:16:58,327
I won't let you go back to them.

257
00:16:59,087 --> 00:17:00,467
Just hear what I have to say.

258
00:17:00,547 --> 00:17:00,987
Stop!

259
00:17:00,987 --> 00:17:04,627
They're my family, just like you are.

260
00:17:09,347 --> 00:17:11,467
I think I've met the people you're talking about.

261
00:17:11,467 --> 00:17:12,607
You have?

262
00:17:12,727 --> 00:17:13,527
Tell me everything.

263
00:17:13,647 --> 00:17:14,547
Where did you see them?

264
00:17:16,387 --> 00:17:17,867
Hey, answer me.

265
00:17:19,827 --> 00:17:21,567
Earlier, there was a girl.

266
00:17:22,047 --> 00:17:23,567
She and her friends saved my life.

267
00:17:24,187 --> 00:17:25,187
She fought with a scythe.

268
00:17:25,187 --> 00:17:26,487
That's them.

269
00:17:26,887 --> 00:17:28,407
I told you they're good guys.

270
00:17:28,607 --> 00:17:28,907
Right?

271
00:17:29,107 --> 00:17:29,447
Right?

272
00:17:29,707 --> 00:17:31,327
That means we should be helping them out.

273
00:17:31,527 --> 00:17:31,867
Right?

274
00:17:32,107 --> 00:17:32,467
Yeah?

275
00:17:36,647 --> 00:17:37,767
Only your friends.

276
00:17:38,247 --> 00:17:39,407
I'll help the four of them.

277
00:17:39,747 --> 00:17:40,567
That's great.

278
00:17:40,867 --> 00:17:41,727
Hey, what are you doing?

279
00:17:41,807 --> 00:17:42,327
Cut it out.

280
00:17:42,467 --> 00:17:43,867
All right, let's get out of here.

281
00:17:43,947 --> 00:17:45,067
We've got work to do.

282
00:17:45,547 --> 00:17:46,587
Where do you think they are?

283
00:17:47,187 --> 00:17:48,447
I don't know for sure.

284
00:17:48,887 --> 00:17:51,727
But I did hear them say something about meeting at an airport.

285
00:18:00,587 --> 00:18:02,207
So, what's going on, Shinwa?

286
00:18:02,487 --> 00:18:04,307
I don't know anything more than you do.

287
00:18:05,027 --> 00:18:07,067
I thought there were supposed to be helicopters.

288
00:18:07,627 --> 00:18:09,047
But this place is deserted.

289
00:18:09,787 --> 00:18:11,467
There aren't even any cars around.

290
00:18:16,587 --> 00:18:21,147
I could have driven, you know.

291
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:22,107
I'm good at it.

292
00:18:22,247 --> 00:18:24,727
I thought you said you wanted us both to survive.

293
00:18:25,007 --> 00:18:25,647
Oh, shut up.

294
00:18:26,787 --> 00:18:27,227
So?

295
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:29,347
You wanted to talk?

296
00:18:29,967 --> 00:18:30,367
Right.

297
00:18:35,447 --> 00:18:37,347
The humans have ulterior motives.

298
00:18:37,347 --> 00:18:40,027
They're using you as a test subject for experimentation.

299
00:18:40,727 --> 00:18:41,467
Is that all?

300
00:18:41,527 --> 00:18:42,547
I already knew that.

301
00:18:42,667 --> 00:18:45,027
The experiment will have far-reaching consequences.

302
00:18:45,027 --> 00:18:50,027
And as a result, humans and vampires across the globe are targeting you.

303
00:18:50,587 --> 00:18:51,807
Humans and vampires?

304
00:18:52,147 --> 00:18:54,467
Wow, I had no idea I was so popular.

305
00:18:54,887 --> 00:18:55,787
This is serious.

306
00:18:56,327 --> 00:18:58,547
It's the same experiment that messed up the world.

307
00:18:59,187 --> 00:19:01,307
The reason all of the adults died years ago.

308
00:19:01,987 --> 00:19:03,507
It almost made humans extinct.

309
00:19:04,307 --> 00:19:05,367
Hold up a second.

310
00:19:05,967 --> 00:19:08,627
Are you saying it's my fault the world was almost destroyed?

311
00:19:09,487 --> 00:19:10,227
No, you.

312
00:19:10,527 --> 00:19:11,847
We didn't do any of this.

313
00:19:12,327 --> 00:19:14,247
We were innocent kids who were being used.

314
00:19:14,247 --> 00:19:16,247
Humans are the ones who caused this.

315
00:19:17,467 --> 00:19:20,527
The Hyakuya orphanage where we lived was nothing but a laboratory.

316
00:19:21,307 --> 00:19:25,427
After it was gone, the Japanese Imperial Demon Army took over the experimentation.

317
00:19:29,807 --> 00:19:32,287
The experiment's called Seraph of the End.

318
00:19:32,287 --> 00:19:35,847
Humans are ugly creatures.

319
00:19:35,847 --> 00:19:37,927
They're animals driven by greed.

320
00:19:38,167 --> 00:19:39,947
They only want to make themselves stronger.

321
00:19:40,507 --> 00:19:42,127
They'll hurt anyone to get more power.

322
00:19:42,307 --> 00:19:44,347
I can't leave you in the hands of people like that.

323
00:19:47,347 --> 00:19:49,367
Mika, I'm also a human.

324
00:19:49,367 --> 00:19:54,907
And if it's at all possible, I want to turn you back into one too.

325
00:19:55,907 --> 00:19:58,587
So it's not like you can say all of humanity is bad.

326
00:19:58,947 --> 00:20:03,227
If the wrong people have you under their control, they could use you to end this world in a heartbeat.

327
00:20:03,227 --> 00:20:07,947
Run away with me instead.

328
00:20:10,827 --> 00:20:14,727
We'll make a new home somewhere secluded, far away from this warp.

329
00:20:14,727 --> 00:20:17,047
Where no one can find us.

330
00:20:17,727 --> 00:20:19,867
The vampires or the moon demon company.

331
00:20:21,447 --> 00:20:22,267
That's right.

332
00:20:22,267 --> 00:20:29,767
This reminds me of another time.

333
00:20:31,307 --> 00:20:35,667
Remember how we ran away from the vampires because we thought we could find paradise somewhere else?

334
00:20:35,907 --> 00:20:36,187
Yeah.

335
00:20:36,647 --> 00:20:37,547
But it didn't work.

336
00:20:37,767 --> 00:20:40,427
Everyone got killed and we learned that paradise didn't exist.

337
00:20:40,987 --> 00:20:42,307
Instead, there's only one thing.

338
00:20:43,887 --> 00:20:44,747
This world.

339
00:20:46,887 --> 00:20:49,407
I don't think there's anywhere else left for us to go.

340
00:20:50,627 --> 00:20:52,067
Isn't it worth looking, though?

341
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:54,847
If so, then we can discuss that with my friends.

342
00:20:55,827 --> 00:20:56,607
They're smart.

343
00:20:56,727 --> 00:20:59,287
They can help us run away if that's what you really want us to do.

344
00:21:00,847 --> 00:21:02,747
And you're certain we can trust them, you?

345
00:21:03,047 --> 00:21:04,107
Sure, don't worry.

346
00:21:04,727 --> 00:21:05,807
They're the good guys.

347
00:21:06,567 --> 00:21:08,427
Trust them just as much as you trust me.

348
00:21:08,847 --> 00:21:09,187
Okay?

349
00:21:22,267 --> 00:21:28,407
They're the good guys.

350
00:21:34,807 --> 00:21:46,847
They're the good guys.

351
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:48,847
You

352
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:34,987
Next time on Seraph of the End, Arrogant Love.

